@page "/"
<h3>Welcome to ExpenseCategorizer</h3>

<p class="text-muted">
    AI‑powered categorization with human correction built‑in.
    Track, categorize, and report your expenses with ease.
    Here’s how to get started:
</p>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>
            <img src="images/upload.png" alt="Upload Icon" style="height:50px; margin-right:8px; vertical-align:middle; margin-bottom: 6px" />
            1. Upload Expense</h5>
        <p>
            Upload receipts, PDFs, images, or JSON files.
            OCR extracts text, rule‑based parsing captures amounts, and ML.NET predicts categories with explanations from Azure OpenAI.
            Optimized for handwritten receipts; complex invoices may need correction.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="/upload">Go to Upload</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>
            <img src="images/dashboard.png" alt="Dashboard Icon" style="height:50px; margin-right:8px; vertical-align:middle; margin-bottom: 6px" />
            2. Get All Expenses</h5>
        <p>
            View your expense dashboard with categories, explanations, dates, and amounts.
            Rows with Amount = 0 are flagged for correction, ensuring data integrity even when OCR parsing is imperfect.
            Edit or delete entries directly from the table.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="/dashboard">View Expenses</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>
            <img src="images/report.png" alt="Report Icon" style="height:50px; margin-right:8px; vertical-align:middle; margin-bottom: 6px" />
            3. Download Monthly Report</h5>
        <p>
            Generate a PDF report of your expenses for the month.
            Perfect for bookkeeping or sharing with clients.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="/report">Download Report</a>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Embed FAQ component -->
<div class="mt-5">
    <FAQ />
</div>
